virglrenderer: copy only the decoded picture of AV1 and VP9 frames

What: the copy of a decoded frame into the guest's plane textures takes the
picture's size from the picture description (AV1's and VP9's frame_width and
frame_height) where it is smaller than the frame VideoToolbox returned; the
plane-edge fill then repeats the picture's last row and column past it. With
OMACVM_VIDEO_DEBUG=1 qemu.log says each new "output WxH, picture WxH".
Why: VideoToolbox's AV1 frame is as large as the format description, which
av1_set_format makes from max_width + 1 and max_height + 1. Mesa's VA frontend
sends the surface's size there (picture_av1.c), not the size minus one, and
Chrome's surfaces are its coded size (rounded up to 16): the frame came back
larger than the picture, its extra rows (not the picture's, near zero) were
copied as picture, and the fill was skipped. In Google Chrome's hardware
decoding AV1 at 1080p, 540p and 360p had the green bar again (8, 4 and 8 rows).
Applies on top of virgl-videotoolbox-decode.patch and
virgl-video-plane-edge.patch.
Upstreamable with the decode backend; not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-video-padding.c, the AV1 case with Mesa's max_width and
max_height (the 320x192 surface): without the patch the 4800 texels past the
picture are not its last row and column; GPU and CPU copy.
